WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.000
Narrator: Disney released
the second trailer

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.130
for its remake of the
classic film "The Lion King."

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.950
In it we get a glimpse
of the main characters,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.610
and we finally get to
hear some of them speak

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.290
for the very first time.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.860
Though the film is still
technically animated,

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.310
this version is a more
photo-realistic take on the story.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.680
There are also lots of shots that mirror

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.540
the original animated film.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.490
Here is everything you might have missed.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.710
The trailer opens with
young Simba and Nala

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.165
walking through the Elephant Graveyard.

00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:36.740
This is the wasteland beyond the borders

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.438
of the Pride Land where
Simba is told not to go.

00:00:40.438 --> 00:00:42.480
Mufasa: You must never go there, Simba.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.191
Narrator: It's also the home
of the three hyena villains,

00:00:45.191 --> 00:00:48.220
Shenzi, Banzai, and Ed.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.984
We hear Scar, voiced by
Chiwetel Ejiofor, say...

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:55.130
Scar: Life's not fair.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.620
Narrator: A classic line from the film

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.460
in which he's talking to a
mouse that he's about to eat.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.430
Scar: Life's not fair, is it?

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.870
Narrator: While the Scar in the new film

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.220
seems to have the same
scar over his left eye,

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.910
he has a piece of flesh
missing from his right ear.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.020
He also doesn't have the
green eyes from the cartoon,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.210
which makes sense since
the movie is going for

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:17.800
a more realistic look.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.230
Next, we see a shot straight
out of the original film

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.050
with the birds flying over
the water of the Pride Lands

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.343
and Simba on top of the cliff
with his father, Mufasa.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.510
James Earl Jones reprises his role

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.296
as the voice in the remake.

00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:36.420
Mufasa: A true king searches

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.523
for what he can give.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.290
Narrator: The trailer also
gives us our first look

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.765
at Zazu, the red-billed hornbill,

00:01:42.765 --> 00:01:45.220
voiced by comedian John Oliver.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:49.200
He's the majordomo or chief
steward to King Mufasa.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.140
Mufasa: What am I going to do with him?

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.060
Zazu: He'd make a very handsome throw rug.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.100
Narrator: We also see a
pretty close shot-for-shot

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.060
version of the scene just
after the Elephant Graveyard

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.800
in which Mufasa and Zazu are leading Simba

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.980
and Nala back home in shame.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.143
There's even a recreation
of the iconic moment

00:02:05.143 --> 00:02:08.463
when young Simba puts his
paw in his father's print.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.410
We also see the wildebeest
stampede orchestrated by Scar,

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.323
which results in the death of Mufasa,

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.990
and Scar telling Simba...

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.513
Scar: Run away, Simba, and never return.

00:02:29.832 --> 00:02:32.797
Scar: Run away and never return.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.870
Narrator: Two more memorable characters

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.000
we get a first look at in the new trailer

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.530
are the meerkat, Timon,
and warthog, Pumbaa,

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:45.500
voiced by Billy Eichner and Seth Rogen.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.620
We see them walking with Simba
in an almost exact recreation

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.380
of the original scene,
a time-lapse of Simba

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.585
growing older during "Hakuna Matata."

00:02:53.585 --> 00:02:55.600
Timon: Hakuna Matata!

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.650
Narrator: While the trailer
shows Simba eyeing a beetle,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.763
in the original, Pumbaa is
the one chasing the bug.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.560
After Simba and Nala finally reunite,

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.060
they are seen drinking water together,

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.090
which you might remember during the song,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.050
"Can You Feel the Love Tonight."

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:16.380
We see almost the exact same
scene in the new trailer.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.120
The adult versions of these characters

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.763
will be voiced by Donald Glover
and Beyoncé Knowles-Carter.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.670
Meanwhile, Rafiki is painting

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.050
a red mane around Simba's image.

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.700
In the original film, he does this

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.970
when he realizes Simba is
still alive and is now matured.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.820
After Scar dies and Simba reclaims

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.860
his rightful spot on the throne,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.363
we see him walk up the cliff
and roar in the pouring rain,

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.300
another scene nearly
identical to the original.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.030
The trailer basically gives us
a taste of what we can expect

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.760
from start to finish.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.074
While we don't hear any of
the famous musical numbers,

00:03:53.074 --> 00:03:55.260
there's a slight tease at the end.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.085
We hear a snippet of Timon and Pumbaa

00:03:57.085 --> 00:03:58.909
singing "In the Jungle"

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.645
just as they did in the original.

00:04:00.645 --> 00:04:02.536
♪ In the jungle ♪
♪ A-weema-weh, a-weema-weh ♪

00:04:02.536 --> 00:04:04.674
♪ The mighty jungle ♪
♪ A-weema-weh, a-weema-weh ♪

00:04:04.674 --> 00:04:07.632
♪ A-weema-weh, a-weema-weh,
a-weema-weh, a-weema-weh ♪

00:04:07.632 --> 00:04:11.000
♪ A-weema-weh, a-weema-weh,
a-weema-weh, a-weema-weh ♪

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.080
Narrator: We can likely expect to see more

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.350
and hear more of the music from
the film in the days to come

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.283
ahead of the movie's release in July 2019.

